  "footnote": "Source: Autonomy et al., UK pilot report, Feb 2023, self-reported. \"Better\" includes a slower pace and a lighter workload",
  "notes": "Staff in the 61 UK pilot companies felt both sides. 71% reported less burnout, 39% less stress and 40% fewer sleep problems. But 62% said the pace of work rose, only 2% said it slowed, and 20% said their workload grew. Hours also fell by less than a full day: self-reported weekly hours went from 38 to 34. Brazil saw the same pattern, with 48.2% of staff feeling a faster pace and a third of the companies hiring to cope. That is why we cut meetings and process first rather than squeezing five days of work into four."
